  "criteriaResults": {
    "Workspace owner has implicit access to every board in owned projects; nonowners need both active project membership and an explicit active grant on the specific board, and keep their project role's action limits.": "pass",
    "Migration creates no automatic board grants for existing members; invitations and project membership do not grant board access. Re-adding a removed member does not reactivate old grants.": "pass",
    "Only the owner of the board's workspace can administer board grants. Reject self-elevation, foreign boards, nonmember targets and cross-project access without disclosing hidden resource existence.": "pass",
    "Project managers retain permission to create boards in granted projects but cannot grant board access; a created board does not automatically grant access to its creator or other project members.": "pass",
    "Project-level identity remains visible to authorized project members with zero boards; board list and all board-related reads and counts exclude ungranted boards before pagination or aggregation.": "pass",
    "All mounted board/card/column, comments/activity, images/uploads, imports, trash, notifications, search, tasks, retries and replay entry points enforce the new boundary, including Node and Worker paths.": "pass",
    "Revocation serializes with in-flight writes, import commits and image finalization; revoked actors cannot obtain private data via stale IDs, cursors, caches, retries or idempotency receipts.": "pass",
    "PostgreSQL migration supports clean install and documented safe restart/upgrade; existing sensitive data is not touched. Test against isolated disposable PostgreSQL, never live data.": "pass",
    "Mounted-handler negative tests cover owner, manager, member, viewer, outsider, removed user, stale board grant, sibling/foreign resources, invited owner in another workspace and revocation races.": "pass",
    "Typecheck, build, mandatory integration suites and contracts pass on the exact target; a fresh independent review meets every BACKEND_REVIEW_GATE.md category and blocker rule.": "pass"
